{"repositoryId":430771907,"availability":"available","full":"Divine-Star-Software/DivineVoxelEngine","name":"DivineVoxelEngine","description":"A multi-threaded, renderer-independent voxel engine in TypeScript. Build Minecraft-style voxel worlds and games that run in the browser.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":265,"forks":23,"created":"2021-11-22T15:55:50Z","updated":"2026-09-20T21:18:36Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["babylonjs","minecraft","typescript-library","voxel-game","webgl"],"demo":"https://stackblitz.com/edit/dve-demos","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.514Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.514Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.514Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.514Z","stars":265,"forks":23}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A multi-threaded, renderer-independent voxel engine in TypeScript.","Build Minecraft-style voxel worlds and games that run in the browser.","Try the live demo · Browse the Vlox demos · Getting Started guide"],"features":["Renderer-independent core. The voxel engine lives in @divinevoxel/vlox","and knows nothing about a specific renderer. Official renderers exist for Babylon.js (Classic and PBR shaders), with Three.js and WebGPU renderers in development.","Multi-threaded by design. Meshing, world generation, and world updates all","Fast meshing via precomputed rules. Voxel models are exploded into faces,","and every culling and ambient-occlusion relationship is computed once at registration into flat lookup tables. At mesh time the hot loop is cheap array lookups against those tables."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Divine-Star-Software/DivineVoxelEngine/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"afcec0ddf73fd937a8e92753ff9908b28f8111154516d54683b23c1cc312c0b5","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.609Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:48.609Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoe